# Task 3 report — deterministic V5 local variant rendering

## Outcome

Created `core/pit_optimizer_v5/rendering.py` as the only source change. It renders normal
`SourceOperationV5` templates and atomic four-file full-source escapes into deterministic,
manifest-capped `RenderedVariantV5` values without filesystem, Git, subprocess, provider, Docker,
CLI, replay, or market-data behavior. No tests were created or modified.

Focused implementation commit: `7272bdd` (`feat: render optimizer v5 local variants`).

The approved interface correction adds a required keyword-only
`parent_revision: PolicyRevisionIdentityV5` argument to `render_variants()`. The renderer verifies
that the template names that authenticated parent revision and that all four source digests in the
revision exactly match the supplied parent bundle. Child revisions are then derived from rendered
source bytes while preserving the authenticated parent's policy-interface, trusted-runtime, and
immutable-constraint identities. No authority is inferred from an opaque revision digest.

## Implemented contracts

- The parent and every rendered result are exact ordered `SourceBundleV5` four-file bundles.
  Constructing each `SourceFileV5` invokes the extracted source parse/compile/public-export
  validator, and `RenderedVariantV5` verifies that the derived revision identifies the exact
  rendered bytes.
- Normal operations replace only an authorized complete public function or uppercase module
  constant. Parent target spans are located syntactically, whole physical statement lines are
  replaced, and duplicate/overlapping operations fail closed.
- The full-source escape is accepted only when its entire four-file content can be reconstructed
  from the authenticated parent by replacing exactly the declared authorized symbols. Any byte
  change elsewhere, including path/import/module-level changes, is rejected.
- Every declared axis must have exactly one syntactically valid `PIT_AXIS("name")` call inside its
  authorized function or constant value. Missing, duplicated, unknown, malformed, or out-of-scope
  markers fail; tokenizer inspection ensures no executable marker name remains after rendering.
- Marker calls are replaced by their exact source spans, never with `ast.unparse`. Canonical
  parenthesized Python literals preserve strict `bool`/`int`/finite-`float`/`str` types and numeric
  precedence while leaving unrelated source bytes untouched. AST UTF-8 byte columns are converted
  safely to Python string offsets.
- Parent and child import ASTs must match exactly and imports must remain top-level. Together with
  the full-source reconstruction rule, this prevents normal-operation and escape-mode import
  expansion while preserving parent formatting outside target spans.
- Assignment enumeration emits the declared default first, one-axis-at-a-time deviations next in
  declared axis/value order, and remaining Cartesian assignments ordered by canonical assignment
  identity. Scheduling-tier duplicates are removed with strict type-aware keys, and the cap applies
  to emitted unique assignments.
- A default whose rendered bytes and policy identity equal the parent is deliberately emitted for
  downstream `exact_duplicate` classification. If two distinct strict assignments render identical
  complete bundles, `VariantRenderingCollisionV5` fails closed instead of collapsing them.
- Repeating a render with identical inputs returns byte-identical ordered variants.

The reusable extracted V5 source service is deliberately structural: syntax, compilation, async
top-level rejection, and exact public exports. V5 import and authoring authority are enforced here
and in `policy_scope.py`; introducing a broader V3 policy-language purity validator is outside the
approved Task 3 one-file boundary.

